xnu: 0196 vince Pronto: wait up to 30 s for WCNSS_CTRL

0195 on the phone: RPM switched the Iris rails on (L9, L19 now ON) and the RF
clock buffers, but with the Iris XO at 48 MHz the firmware still had no
WCNSS_CTRL after 5 s (no crash reason), and at 19.2 MHz HAL_START answers 38.
With a powered Iris the firmware may calibrate first: wait vincectrlwait s
(default 30) and log when the channel appears.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/vince_smd.c b/bsd/dev/vince_smd.c
index 2c9b1a1..1ab49ce 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/vince_smd.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/vince_smd.c
@@ -668,13 +668,20 @@ vp_ctrl(const uint8_t *nv, uint32_t nv_len)
 	static uint8_t msg[16 + WC_NV_FRAG], rsp[256];
 	int r = -1;
 
-	for (int i = 0; i < 200 && !vince_smd_find("WCNSS_CTRL", &c); i++) {
+	/*
+	 * With the Iris powered and its XO at 48 MHz the firmware may run its RF calibration before it creates the
+	 * channels: wait vincectrlwait seconds (default 30; 0194 gave up after 5 s with no crash reason written).
+	 */
+	int wait_s = 30, waited = 0;
+	(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("vincectrlwait", &wait_s, sizeof(wait_s));
+	for (; waited < wait_s * 40 && !vince_smd_find("WCNSS_CTRL", &c); waited++) {
 		vince_smd_sleep(25);
 	}
 	if (!vince_smd_find("WCNSS_CTRL", &c)) {
-		printf("VINCE PRONTO: no WCNSS_CTRL channel within 5 s\n");
+		printf("VINCE PRONTO: no WCNSS_CTRL channel within %d s\n", wait_s);
 		return -1;
 	}
+	printf("VINCE PRONTO: WCNSS_CTRL appeared after %d ms\n", waited * 25);
 	for (int i = 0; i < 100 && (r = vince_smd_open(&c)) == -1; i++) {
 		vince_smd_sleep(20);
 	}
